{"amendments":[{"body":"`crates/tank_harness/src/calibration.rs:77-81` stores `FieldCheck.observed`, `envelope_min`, and `envelope_max` as raw `f64`s, and `check_classified()` feeds `f64::INFINITY` into that struct for one-sided envelopes such as `do_min()` (`crates/tank_harness/src/calibration.rs:393-394`, `crates/tank_harness/src/calibration.rs:487-538`). `serde_json` serializes `Infinity`/`NaN` as `null`, so `CalibrationReport` no longer round-trips as JSON; `cargo test -p tank_harness --test calibration_report` is already failing in `test_report_machine_readable` and `test_full_calibration_workflow` with `invalid type: null, expected f64`. The report needs a JSON-safe representation for open-ended or non-finite values before it can be considered machine-readable.","rationale":"This is a release-blocking correctness bug: the advertised calibration-report output cannot be parsed back by downstream tooling or even by the crate's own tests."},{"body":"`CalibrationRun::finish()` computes `overall_status` only from `checkpoint_rows` and then ignores the `Result` from `self.inner.finish()` (`crates/tank_harness/src/calibration.rs:321-338`). Because callers can reach the shared harness through `CalibrationRun::inner_mut()` (`crates/tank_harness/src/calibration.rs:251-253`), and the harness exposes additional failure paths such as `assert_snapshot()` and `record_failure()` (`crates/tank_harness/src/lib.rs:580-614`), a calibration run can accumulate real harness failures while the returned `ScenarioRow` still says `pass` and omits `artifact_path`. `finish()` should propagate or incorporate underlying harness failures instead of dropping them.","rationale":"A scientific validation report must not silently convert real failures into passes; that would make tuning decisions and release notes untrustworthy."}],"summary":"Reviewed the tracked diff and the newly exported calibration module end-to-end. The shrimp probe carbonate-state updates look coherent and their test suite passes, but I found two correctness blockers in calibration reporting: JSON round-tripping is broken for one-sided/non-finite bounds, and calibration runs can silently mask underlying harness failures."}